2. Definitions

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
agreement. An individual acting for an employer or client acts for that
entity, rather than in an individual capacity.

"Organization Group" means You and all entities that control, are
controlled by, or are under common control with You. Control means owning
more than half the voting rights or otherwise directing management.

"Personnel" means the number of employees, full-time and part-time, plus
individual contractors regularly working in employee-equivalent roles,
across the Organization Group. A person is counted once, not once per role.

"Customers" means distinct external individuals or legal entities with an
active paid subscription, service contract, or purchase during the preceding
12 months, across the Organization Group. Count each customer once. This
count covers the whole business, not only the product using GoiBERT, and
does not count an unpaid visitor or an unconverted free registration.

"Commercial Use" means use in operating a business, providing products or
services to others, serving paying customers, or supporting internal
business operations. Customer deployment by a consultant is use on behalf
of the customer as well as the consultant.

"Research and Evaluation" means teaching, academic study, noncommercial
scientific research, or an isolated internal evaluation of whether to adopt
GoiBERT. It excludes production deployment, operational business use,
customer-facing pilots and delivery of work for a paying client. A business
may evaluate the models internally without qualifying for production use.

"Model Derivatives" means modified, fine-tuned, quantized or otherwise
adapted versions of the GoiBERT Materials, to the extent they incorporate
Licensor's protected contributions. Merely receiving a classification,
embedding or other ordinary inference output does not make an independent
application a Model Derivative. This definition does not assert ownership
of Your independent code or of ordinary inference outputs.

3. Community permission

Subject to this agreement and the applicable upstream terms, Licensor
grants You a worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free copyright license to
download, reproduce, run, evaluate, modify and distribute the GoiBERT
Materials and Model Derivatives for:

  (a) Research and Evaluation; or
  (b) Commercial Use while the Organization Group has BOTH fewer than
      100 Personnel AND fewer than 1,000 Customers.

The permission covers local inference, hosted inference and integration
into Your products or internal systems, within those limits. You may charge
for permitted products or services. You must have authority to accept this
agreement for the entity on whose behalf You act.

4. Enterprise commercial agreement

If either threshold is reached — 100 or more Personnel OR 1,000 or more
Customers — this agreement does not authorize Commercial Use. Obtain a
separate written commercial agreement from Licensor before starting or
continuing that use. Research and Evaluation remains available under
Section 3(a), subject to all upstream terms.

Do not divide deployment between affiliates, contractors or resellers to
avoid these thresholds. A small service provider cannot use its own size
to authorize an enterprise customer's deployment. An enterprise agreement
may state different commercial terms for Licensor's contributions, but
cannot waive upstream obligations without the relevant rights holder's
authorization.

Fees, if any, are determined in the separate signed agreement. Crossing a
threshold does not by itself establish a debt, an automatic subscription,
or acceptance of an unspecified price. If You become ineligible, cease
Commercial Use unless and until an enterprise agreement authorizes it.

5. Redistribution and attribution

When distributing the GoiBERT Materials or Model Derivatives:

  (a) include this agreement, NOTICE and all applicable upstream license
      texts and copyright, attribution and disclaimer notices;
  (b) identify modifications and avoid representing a modified model as an
      unmodified official GoiBERT release;
  (c) state that each recipient must qualify independently for community
      Commercial Use or obtain a separate enterprise agreement; and
  (d) do not grant rights to Licensor's contributions beyond those You have.

You may license Your independent modifications separately, subject to the
continuing obligations for the materials they incorporate. There is no
requirement here to publish Your independent application source code.
Providing access through an API does not remove Your own obligations.

Retain the project attribution and upstream notices. Academic citation is
requested in publications; no additional on-screen logo obligation is
created by this agreement. Names and logos may not imply endorsement.

